===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Hallowe'en}}

===Etymology===
A shortening of ''[[All Hallows'|All-Hallow]]-[[even#Etymology 2|even]]'', ''All Hallows’ Eve'' (the name of the evening before [[All Saints Day]]).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌhæləʊˈiːn/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˌhæləˈwiːn/|/ˌhɑləˈwiːn/|/ˌhæləʊˈiːn/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-Halloween.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|s}}

# The [[eve]] of [[All Hallows' Day]]; 31st [[October]]; celebrated (mostly in the [[United Kingdom]], [[Canada]], [[United States]] and [[Ireland]]) by [[children]] going [[door-to-door]] in [[costume]] and demanding [[candy]] with [[menace]]s.

